chunk_findings.detail:
Only the session-entries path clips text (`_clip(kept, cut)`); the list path returns the body verbatim:
```
if body.get("truncated") is True and isinstance(body.get("rows"), list):
    return body, ("truncated: showing ...")
```
For any `kind` whose rows carry free text (notably `kind=search`, whose whole point is returning matched record text/snippets, and `kind=bug`/`kind=research` with description fields), nothing bounds the per-row text. A search hit whose matched text is, say, 10 KB is emitted in full because this branch neither clips the rows nor relies on `view_read` having clipped them (the function's own docstring only claims rows "arrive already cut by `limit`" — i.e. cut by count, not clipped by length). The session path demonstrates the intended bounding, so the list kinds silently escape it and can exceed the MCP payload budget the change is supposed to enforce with `mcp_bound`.

